# Backend BASE URL (Spring Boot) — NO `/api` suffix. `axiosClient.js` adds the suffix, so
# the prefix exists in exactly one place. Both realtime sockets are built from this value
# too (`src/lib/wsUrl.js`).
#
# VITE_API_URL is baked into the bundle at BUILD time, not read at runtime, so changing it
# requires a rebuild. That is why each environment gets its own value:
#
#   development   `.env`              empty                  (the dev server proxies)
#   production    Cloudflare Pages    https://<deployed host>
#
# THE PRODUCTION VALUE GOES IN THE CLOUDFLARE DASHBOARD, NOT IN A FILE HERE — and this is
# the part that costs people an afternoon. `.gitignore` drops BOTH `.env` and
# `.env.production`, so a build that clones this repo has NEITHER: the value comes out
# undefined, an undefined base resolves against the page's own origin, and the deployed
# site quietly calls `https://<the pages domain>/api/...` with nothing logged. Editing a
# file on your machine cannot fix that, because the file is never pushed.
#
#   Workers & Pages -> this project -> Settings -> Environment variables -> Production
#   VITE_API_URL = https://<backend host>        (BASE url, NO /api suffix)
#
# AS DEPLOYED: the site is https://dev.enpractice.site and the backend is
# https://enpractice-api.swpts.site, so the value there is
# `VITE_API_URL=https://enpractice-api.swpts.site`. The backend's CORS allowlist and its two
# socket allowlists are a SEPARATE, matching list — verified: that origin gets
# `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` on REST and a 101 handshake on `/ws/realtime-chat`. A
# `*.pages.dev` origin is rejected on both, so a preview deployment needs its own entry
# there. `https://www.enpractice.site` is not in the list either.
#
# then REDEPLOY: the value is inlined during the build, so adding the variable does not
# change a deployment that already exists. A real env var outranks every `.env` file.
#
# `vite.config.js` fails the build outright when `CF_PAGES` is set and the value is empty,
# relative or localhost, so this mistake can no longer ship silently. Committing
# `.env.production` is the supported alternative (the value is public — it is baked into
# the bundle every visitor downloads) and makes the build reproducible from git alone.
# That is why `.env.production` is listed in `.gitignore`; delete that line if you take
# that route.
#
# EMPTY means SAME ORIGIN: the Vite dev server proxies /api and /ws to the backend
# (vite.config.js §4), so the page is same-origin with itself. An absolute
# http://localhost:8082 here breaks the two sockets — `resolveWsUrl()` would yield
# `ws://localhost:8082/ws/...` on a page served over https, which the browser blocks as
# mixed content before the first frame is sent. REST keeps answering (the backend's CORS
# allowlist covers localhost on any port), which is what makes the fault hard to read.
#
# Vite reads `.env` in EVERY mode and lets `.env.<mode>` override it, so `.env.production`
# only needs to carry VITE_API_URL — unless the build box has no `.env`, in which case it
# needs a copy of every other key below.
VITE_API_URL=
VITE_INTERNAL_KEY=internal-key

# Public site URL, used for canonical / og:url / absolute og:image.
VITE_SITE_URL=https://enpractice.site

# Firebase (FCM push notifications). Fill in from the Firebase console.
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=firebase-api-key
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=project-id.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=project-id
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=project-id.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=app-id
VITE_FIREBASE_VAPID_KEY=vapid-key
